  "query_preview": "(This evening through Sunday)...\nIssued at 215 PM EDT Sun Sep 27 2026\n\nRest of This Afternoon through Tuesday...\n\nSubsidence on the west side of the upper low on the east coast of \nthe USA along with surface high pressure will continue to provide \ndry and quiet weather for central Indiana.\n\nMainly some passing high clouds are expected, especially across the \nwestern forecast area. Good radiational cooling will occur tonight \nand Monday night, so have cut blended guidance's temperatures both \nnights. These conditions will allow for patchy fog once again late \ntonight/early Monday and late Monday night/early Tuesday.\n\nWith the dry atmosphere in place and plentiful sunshine expected, \nraised Monday's and Tuesday's highs from blended guidance.\n\nWednesday through Next Weekend...\n\nA northern stream upper trough will move through Canada and the \nGreat Lakes into Friday, and this will bring a surface front into \nthe area by Friday.\n\nMeanwhile, an upper low across the southwestern USA will gradually \nmove northeast. This low will have taken in tropical remnants and \nwill thus have good moisture with it. A surface low pressure system \nwill accompany the upper system. \n\nThe upper low will weaken as it moves north and east, but guidance \ncontinues to differ on its speed and what happens with it. Some \nguidance has the northern stream absorb the remnants of the upper \nlow while others keep the upper low separate and farther southwest. \nThis also affects the eventual location of the associated surface \nlow pressure system. Thus, there is higher uncertainty in the \nforecast for later this week.\n\nIt now appears forcing will arrive later than previously thought, so \nWednesday looks dry during the day. Otherwise, rain chances will be \naround Thursday into next weekend. With the uncertainty, confidence \nin timing and location of the highest PoPs remains low. With the \nweakening upper low still having tropical moisture, locally heavy \nrain will be a threat late week.\n\nWith the slower arrival of the system, well above normal \ntemperatures (upper 80s not out of the question for parts of the \narea) will continue into Thursday. Afterward, clouds/rain/cooler air \nbehind a front will lead to below normal temperatures next weekend.",
